  "notes": "MERGE NOTE: institution.kind corrected from worker value private4yr to community (Quincy College is a public, two-year municipally affiliated community college in Quincy, MA, licensed to grant baccalaureate degrees). Transcribed from Quincy College's official 'COMPUTER SCIENCE Bachelor of Science Degree Semester Path' PDF (https://quincycollege.edu/wp-content/uploads/Computer-Science-Bachelors-Semester-Path-2025.pdf), the current semester-path document published under the 2025-2026 Course Catalog at https://quincycollege.edu/quincy-college-catalog-2025-2026/. Catalog year: 2025-2026. Transcription method: PDF downloaded from quincycollege.edu, extracted with pdftotext, then every semester table verified cell-by-cell against PNG page renders (catalog pp. 127-128). No courses, credits, or prerequisites invented. Caveats: (1) Either/or prerequisites appear in the source as 'CSI 104 or CSI 116' (CSI 107, CSI 235, CSI 311, CSA 229). CSI 104 is in the plan; CSI 116 is not, so CSI 116 is listed in external_prereqs and both codes appear in each prereq list; the either/or is documented here. (2) MAT 103 prints 'Appropriate Placement Score or Completion of MAT 097'; the placement alternative is documented here and MAT 097 is in external_prereqs. (3) MAT 113 prints 'MAT 103 or Permission of Instructor'; the permission alternative is documented here. (4) Semester 6: the second Open Elective* row has 'CSI 218' printed in the Pre-Requisites column of the source document; transcribed verbatim (the source's own row alignment). (5) CSI 480 prints 'CSI 218; MAT 210 (pre or coreq)'; MAT 210 is carried as a prereq and the pre-or-coreq is documented here. (6) CSI 490 prints 'CSI 218, 226, 330 & 315', expanded to full course codes. Footnotes from the source: '*At least 3 open elective credits must be 300-level or above'; '**At least 3 program elective credits must be 300-level or above'; '***Choose six credits from General Education Elective course list, not CSI or CSA, starting page 99. BUS 220 Business Ethics recommended. Three credits must be 300-level or above.' Catalog publishes 'Total credits required for graduation 120 credits'; the semester path totals (15+15+16+16+15+16+15+12) sum to exactly 120 - no discrepancy. Quincy College offers associate, certificate, and bachelor's degrees (Computer Science is a BS here, with 48 bachelor students per the July 2026 Factbook); institution kind set to private4yr, not 'cc', since the credential is a bachelor's degree.",
